cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LexiCore-5000, please cite the dataset and the corpus evidence behind it."
title: "LexiCore-5000: an open, evidence-ranked English core vocabulary list (A1-C1)"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/X-Trivle/LexiCore"
url: "https://github.com/X-Trivle/LexiCore"
abstract: >-
  5,000 single-token English headwords, 1,000 per CEFR band (A1-C1), selected by a weighted
  score over frequency, document dispersion, source balance and teaching-list utility measured
  on 13,632,611,970 words from five corpora (FineWeb sample/10BT, FineWeb-Edu-score-2,
  Wikipedia 20231101.en, OPUS-OpenSubtitles v2024, Common Crawl CC-MAIN-2026-34). Levels come
  from CEFR-J v1.5 and the Octanove C1/C2 profile where published, and from a calibrated
  multinomial logistic model for the remainder. Released under CC BY 4.0; see the repository's
  KNOWN_ISSUES for the axes (recency, POS) that are not reliable in this version.
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - name: "The LexiCore maintainers"
    entity: true
keywords:
  - english
  - vocabulary
  - cefr
  - wordlist
  - frequency list
  - corpus linguistics
  - language learning
preferred-citation:
